    "found": "Elder abuse does not just apply to those who are older than 65 years old. A “dependent adult” is someone who is between the ages of 16 and 64, has some form of either physical or mental disability, and either needs assistance with daily tasks or lives in a 24-hour care facility. Both elders and dependent adults who have suffered some form of abuse have the right to file an elder abuse claim."
